":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-09-17T22:39:14Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T23:29:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.5.stable.official [876b29033]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.6.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M3 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M3 Pro (12 threads) - 18.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nDuplicating a node tree that contains a node that references another node inside the same tree (e.g. via an exported var) when the referenced node name contains an @ symbol breaks that link in the duplicated node.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a parent node with 2 children, add a reference from one child to the other (e.g. via an exported var)\n2. Ensure referenced child node uses default name (contains @ symbol)\n3. duplicate() the parent node\n4. The duplicate child node that referenced the other child won't reference anything\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp-lost-reference-on-duplicate.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22395277/mrp-lost-reference-on-duplicate.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110636/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110636/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}